#!/usr/bin/env python
"""Track B B-WIDTH STEP 1 -- train a WIDTH-objective narrative adapter on the frozen 734a.

Reuses the B1 trainer's canonical data-prep + held-out split + the SAME adapter / injection
point (narrative -> additive memory_states), but ADDS a width objective so the conditioned
ensemble's fan WIDTH tracks the GROUNDED narrative-intensity scalar
(nl_track_b_grounded_intensity, prose-parse, NO OpenAI). The 734a backbone is loaded
read-only, FROZEN, and never written; a separate checkpoint is saved.

Why a differentiable rollout (not a noise-scale head): 734a has
``conditional_base_noise_scale=False`` => ``base_noise_log_scale is None`` => width is produced
ONLY by the frozen velocity ODE acting on i.i.d. base noise, with narrative_context entering
through ``memory_state`` (the same path that carries 734a's validated width-conditioning,
turb/calm 1.229). There is no differentiable width knob. So the width term is computed from a
gradient-enabled mini-rollout (small K members) that MIRRORS ``sample_batched`` exactly but
keeps the adapter in the graph. We deliberately do NOT add a base_noise_scale head: that is a
different mechanism, adds a non-adapter param, and would break the present=False->734a-identity
invariant.

Loss = velocity_matching (B1's training_loss, the path-fidelity anchor; preserves CRPS/Energy)
     + lambda_width * width_term
where width_term encourages a POSITIVE within-batch correlation between grounded_intensity and
the conditioned cross-member width_DELTA (width(present=True) - width(present=False), CRN base
noise) -- a soft, differentiable rank/correlation surrogate -- PLUS a null-anchor: examples
passed present=False must keep the baseline width (this is automatic since the zero-init,
presence-gated adapter outputs zero context when present=False, but we also include a fraction
of present=False examples in the velocity-matching term to anchor the no-op).

The width_term correlates intensity vs width_DELTA, NOT raw width (raw width is regime-confounded;
the marginal narrative effect is the delta). Differentiable rollout uses CRN: the present=True
and present=False arms share the SAME base noise per example, so width_delta isolates the
adapter's effect.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import math
import sys
from pathlib import Path
from typing import Any

import numpy as np
import torch

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[3]
if str(ROOT) not in sys.path:
